==Enemy==
Although Axoloty has a relatively long attack animation and can even miss at times, its attacks deal extreme damage, with a 100% chance of creating a Lv.10 [[Wave Attack]]. It has a deceptively high range of 450, enough to outrange and easily destroy most [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]], making them useless unless timed well. However, much like [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]], Axoloty's backswing is so long that it will rarely if ever attack more than once when met with the proper strategy.

Because its attacks are delayed only by backswing, Axoloty will start attacking again right after it flinches for whatever reason (default [[Cat Cannon]]/Breakerblast/Sniper the Cat/other sources of Knockback). It also has a [[Barrier]] with 10,000 HP, which can help to avoid knocking it back.

==Strategy==
Due to how this enemy works, Axoloty will likely never advance after stopping for an attack; for this reason, it is recommended to stop it ASAP to give you time to recover after every attack he does. Fortunately, there are some ways to avoid its attacks. The first is stopping Axoloty close to the enemy base, pushing it behind and forgetting about it completely (only possible if it's not set as a boss, of course). Also be careful when using [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units with more than 10,000 damage per hit, as they may knock it back and reset its attack animation. Avoid using cats with the ability to [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|knockback]] Aliens if its barrier is down.

The second option is using an army focused on many medium-small units and replacing them upon death. In all of Axoloty's [[Cats of the Cosmos]] appearances, this is a viable strategy.

The third option is Wave Shields; [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]] can easily tank hits with its sheer bulk. Other Wave Shields such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] need timing, but it's doable. You only need to keep in mind that whoever gets hit by the regular attack will likely not survive due to Axoloty's long range. [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] also blocks Axoloty's waves well, as his high speed can allow him to easily intercept it.

The last option is knocking back or killing it before it can finish its long attack animation with high-DPS units. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Saw Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] are some non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] options. [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], as well as optionally other [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Alien]] [[:Category:Cats with Freeze ability|Freezers]], can stop Axoloty's movement entirely, giving your units more time to knock it back.

