==Trivia==
*Axoloty is based on the [[wikipedia:Axolotl|axolotl]], a critically endangered species of salamander known for its regenerative abilities and for being fully neotenous, meaning it remains in its larval form without metamorphosing even after reaching adulthood, thus retaining its external gills.
*Axoloty's Japanese name, Looper Looper (ルーパールーパー ''Rūpārūpā''), is derived from ''wooper looper'' (ウーパールーパー ''ūpārūpā''), a Japanese colloquialism for axolotl which originated from a [https://youtu.be/xY5MbCSPapI 1985 Nissin U.F.O marketing campaign] featuring an axolotl named Wooper Looper. This is why Axoloty's Japanese description says it's often sighted near a UFO.
*Axoloty is the opposite of [[Big Sal]]. Where Big Sal is designed specifically to destroy the [[Cat Base]] while ignoring cats, Axoloty's [[Wave Attack]]s can destroy scores of cats but deal no damage to the base.
*Despite its description saying it can blow small Cats into another dimension, Axoloty lacks the Warp ability. It may instead refer to the sheer strength of its attacks, which are practically guaranteed to destroy anything they hit.
*Prior to [[Version 15.0 Update|Version 15.0]], there was a typo in Axoloty's description: instead of saying "its sneezes should be avoided", it said "its sneezes ''are should'' be avoided".

